{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1137022-de2-king-arthur-legend-of-the-sword-movie-as-athur-s-britain-inspiration","id":1137022,"title":"[DE2] King Arthur: Legend of the Sword movie as Athur's Britain inspiration?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-03T13:53:05-07:00","id":1137022,"title":"[DE2] King Arthur: Legend of the Sword movie as Athur's Britain inspiration?","content":"Newest iteration of King Arthur myth by Guy Richie's I avoided like a fire, even if I love this myths. But when I finally seen the movie, I must say it has some strong points from my perspective as inspiration to 6th century England <b>CoD </b>setting. Let's start with the trailer and then I will show my points. Warning, it can have small spoilers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SX9y5JPuRHY\" data-code=\"SX9y5JPuRHY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SX9y5JPuRHY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Points for Dark Eras inspiration:<br /> 1. Pretty good feel of 6th-7th century England. Kingdoms are ruled and modeled by Saxons imitating Roman empire. Just see this great screen from Vortigern throne room.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ha1dCbX.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 2. It reflects the life of common men of that time - if you felt like life in Londinium is very similar to life in Rome few centuries earlier, it\u2019s exactly how it should be. Well, beside very earlier guest Vikings in those places, century or two before their time.<br /> <br /> 3. Mages \u2013 even if open known to royalty and generals \u2013 are force to be reckoned and mostly myth in movie. If Arthurian Dark Era will be Mage in part, I very like the portrayed of sorcerers in the movie \u2013 it really looks like what Awakened would do in Early Middle Ages setting.<br /> <br /> 4. Monsters are\u2026 non-canonical, but also intriguing done.<br /> <br /> Really, see past some minor shortcomings of movie ( like gigantic elephants on opening, straight from <b>Lord of the Rings</b>), and it will give you really interesting and cool feel of this Early Middle Ages England \u2013 that is still after comings of individual Saxon tribes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And not come at me with 'this is much more fantasy than historical piece!' as flaw of this inspiration - in <i>Wolf &amp; Raven</i> there is <b>Elder Scrolls: Skyrim</b> video game mentioned and it's <b><i>glorious</i></b> inspiration for this Era!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}